{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament","id":889231,"title":"Gauging Interest: (Chronicles of) Dark Tournament","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-12T10:39:29-07:00","id":889231,"title":"Gauging Interest: (Chronicles of) Dark Tournament","content":"So, I've been revisiting an old favorite anime, YuYu Hakusho. And I just can't get the idea out of my head of a massive Chronicles of Darkness crossover PvP PbP tournament in the style of so many Shonen anime. I realize it's pure silly nonsense, but I eat that shit up. I can help it. So, I figured, what the hell? There have got to be at least a few folks out there as massively dorky as me who would find this kind of madness appealing. So what say you? Anybody else down for some good ol' over-the-top senseless PvP violence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T06:30:02-07:00","id":891118,"title":"","content":"That sounds pretty crazy to me, id read it! <br /> Hakusho is in my top 3 anime for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7879-kyogetsu","name":"Kyogetsu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:09:15-07:00","id":891259,"title":"","content":"You know I'm actually surprisingly into that idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:14:29-07:00","id":891265,"title":"","content":"While I'm not quite willing to commit yet, I'm interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T15:13:01-07:00","id":891397,"title":"","content":"What good is a game if you can't have some good ol' silly fun every now and again? I'm so down for this! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T19:07:39-07:00","id":891510,"title":"","content":"Something like this could theoretically involve a *lot* of players, but I also figure if we can get at least 5 or 6 players, maybe willing to run multiple characters, that could work too.<br /> <br /> Something that will have to be considered as well is what edition to use. Personally, I much prefer the second edition system. On the other hand, 1st edition has a lot more published options for things like Fighting Styles and Z-Splats. Either way there are a few templates that wouldn't be available without some conversion work, though. That's a bridge we can cross when we come to it, once we've got a better idea what the player base is going to look like, but it's something to consider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T07:05:26-07:00","id":892470,"title":"","content":"I'd love to play this, provided we use 1st edition. I prefer it over 2e and there's the benefit of having a lot more published material for it. But it's your game, so you make the call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T07:29:40-07:00","id":892488,"title":"","content":"This is relevant to my interests, and I would be very interested in playing a character (or more!) in a game/contest/thing like this. I personally prefer 2e mechanics (better balanced), but it would cut a few splats out (depending on when it got run).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T10:19:08-07:00","id":892603,"title":"","content":"I'm not so much interested in the idea, but more I'm interested in see how the mechanics will work in action. I don't know why but now that I'm thinking about it a death battle with re spawns would sounds like a fun game but utterly silly fun. Like pick up a toon, play a week, figureout how it works, putting down when I think of something else. then restarting next time with a different toon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T10:25:07-07:00","id":892607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=892603#post892603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not so much interested in the idea, but more I'm interested in see how the mechanics will work in action. I don't know why but now that I'm thinking about it a death battle with re spawns would sounds like a fun game but utterly silly fun. Like pick up a toon, play a week, figureout how it works, putting down when I think of something else. then restarting next time with a different toon.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be interesting, though not really what I was aiming for with this. That might be something to consider for how to deal with keeping players involved when their characters die or are eliminated though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T11:31:24-07:00","id":892648,"title":"","content":"OH, So maybe at first glance I didn't get the idea. So you're thinking of running, This is the story of the tournament not this game is the tournament? More inline with an anime of dramatic conflicts and special moves, than a tactical battle crunch?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T16:49:41-07:00","id":892871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=892648#post892648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OH, So maybe at first glance I didn't get the idea. So you're thinking of running, This is the story of the tournament not this game is the tournament? More inline with an anime of dramatic conflicts and special moves, than a tactical battle crunch?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, if I just wanted to simulate 1v1 combat I could do that with a dice roller. I'm more interested in running a story for a large group of players that focuses on an anime-style fighting tournament. It would be pretty atypical for a WoD story, with much less focus on horror and drama and much more focus on action and player-versus-player conflict. Ideally, I would like for most or all of the combatants to be player characters, and I would serve as ST and referee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T19:21:02-07:00","id":892946,"title":"","content":"But what is the prize? :O<br /> <br /> (mildly curious)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T19:44:22-07:00","id":892954,"title":"","content":"Also, dibs on Kurama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T23:25:38-07:00","id":893068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=892946#post892946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what is the prize? :O<br /> <br /> (mildly curious)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in Dark Tournament tradition, I suppose the winning team could have a wish granted to each member? I'm open to suggestions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=892954#post892954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, dibs on Kurama.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did have you pegged for a Kurama type. He should be my favorite character, given that his perfect storm of traits that I love in anime characters. And he would be, if it weren't for Hiei.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T06:47:04-07:00","id":893259,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Hiei is always an acceptable exception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T07:13:19-07:00","id":893277,"title":"","content":"What would Kurama be, though? Flowering/Spring Changeling? Thyrsus Mage? Crone Vampire with Mandragora's Garden?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T08:48:19-07:00","id":893350,"title":"","content":"So many things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T13:19:05-07:00","id":893547,"title":"","content":"Any room for a mysterious benefactor who backs a fighter with his extensive resources and Faustian bargains?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T13:21:41-07:00","id":893550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WaywardPaladin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=893547#post893547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any room for a mysterious benefactor who backs a fighter with his extensive resources and Faustian bargains?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T13:28:56-07:00","id":893554,"title":"","content":"Now I need to think what would be the best buffer/support.... Old World Demon would've been rather perfect... I mean, no one here minds giving up their soul for VICTORY right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T13:35:25-07:00","id":893561,"title":"","content":"Okay, let's start grounding this thing out.<br /> <br /> 1) Who is hosting this tournament?<br /> 2) Why are they doing it? What do they get out of it?<br /> 3) Where is it? Why is it there?<br /> 4) Who's funding it? How much is extended to guests, participants, sponsors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-18-2016, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T13:36:37-07:00","id":893563,"title":"","content":"Like, in the case of the Dark Tournament, all of it was done as a way to push Yusuke into becoming a bigger badass, though the Elder Toguro was also using it as an oblation to connect to Hell, if I recall. What's going on here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T18:12:35-07:00","id":893763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=893561#post893561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, let's start grounding this thing out.<br /> <br /> 1) Who is hosting this tournament?<br /> 2) Why are they doing it? What do they get out of it?<br /> 3) Where is it? Why is it there?<br /> 4) Who's funding it? How much is extended to guests, participants, sponsors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, Arc, you're going to make me actually do work for this game? And here I just wanted to see some CofD characters punch each other <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ok, in all seriousness though, I hadn't put a lot of thought into it yet, it was an idea that crossed my mind, so on a whim I started this thread to see if there would be enough folks interested in participating in such a game to pull it off from a logistical perspective. That said, it's looking like I've got a few takers, so it might be time to start working this nebulous concept into an actual story premise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=893563#post893563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, in the case of the Dark Tournament, all of it was done as a way to push Yusuke into becoming a bigger badass, though the Elder Toguro was also using it as an oblation to connect to Hell, if I recall. What's going on here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that was the reason Yuske was invited. Younger Toguro wanted to fight an opponent strong enough to actually challenge him at full power (and it's later revealed he specifically wanted to fight someone strong enough to beat him in a fair fight, as an elaborate form of assisted suicide). But the tournament had been a thing for years before the one featured in the show. In fact, Toguro's whole predicament where he couldn't die naturally and no one was strong enough to kill him was the result of his own wish as prize for winning the same tournament many years before (to become a demon of the highest order, immune to aging, and with absolute strength). The impetus for the tournament itself was just as a way for the Tournament Committee (who may or may not have been the Black Black Club? It wasn't entirely clear, but they at least share some members) to make money off of the betting, as well as to entertain themselves watching demons kill each other. The tunnel to Hell thing was Sakyo's deal, which is how Toguro was able to get a member of the Tournament Committee to go along with his plan to extort Genkai and her protegee (Yuske) into participating. The idea was that Yuske would get stronger over the course of the tournament, kill Toguro in the final round, and Sakyo would make enough money from bets on the tournament to fund his tunnel to Hell project.<br /> <br /> Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaanywhoo.......<br /> <br /> I think the shadow cult of wealthy humans running the show is a pretty good place to start here, although &quot;money and entertainment&quot; is a pretty weak motivation for them. What about the Hototogisu? They could have organized such a thing as a way to get large numbers of supernaturals to congregate, to facilitate relations and trade with influential members of various supernatural societies. I also can't help but be pleased by the idea that this shamelessly anime-inspired crossover game would take place in Japan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T18:21:02-07:00","id":893768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=893763#post893763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aww, Arc, you're going to make me actually do work for this game? And here I just wanted to see some CofD characters punch each other <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ok, in all seriousness though, I hadn't put a lot of thought into it yet, it was an idea that crossed my mind, so on a whim I started this thread to see if there would be enough folks interested in participating in such a game to pull it off from a logistical perspective. That said, it's looking like I've got a few takers, so it might be time to start working this nebulous concept into an actual story premise.<br /> <br /> I think the shadow cult of wealthy humans running the show is a pretty good place to start here, although &quot;money and entertainment&quot; is a pretty weak motivation for them. What about the Hototogisu? They could have organized such a thing as a way to get large numbers of supernaturals to congregate, to facilitate relations and trade with influential members of various supernatural societies. I also can't help but be pleased by the idea that this shamelessly anime-inspired crossover game would take place in Japan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can get behind that. It gives them a neat way to increase the size of their Keiran-Bako and subtly begin expanding their seemingly human-supremacist sales pitch. Supernatural backers will flock in once it reaches a large enough size, lots of ways to manipulate the results to generate something to their purpose. If the tournament is relatively newer, it can also avoid the conflict of overshadowing and destablizing the structure of the conflict while still making it so that backers can put a decent prize out there, seemingly anything a limited imagination could desire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T18:41:55-07:00","id":893777,"title":"","content":"I mean, in terms of &quot;why are we having a pagentized tournament where a bunch of people ritualistically try to kill each other,&quot; I can think of about five cop-out reasons:<br /> <br /> 1) God-Machine occult matrix<br /> 2) True Fae kidnapping<br /> 3) Bored archmage<br /> 4) Recruiting area for secret hunter org/cult<br /> 5) Fact-gathering for secret hunter org/cult<br /> 6) Bored antediluvian wait sorry wrong universe<br /> <br /> That said, I'm all for Hototogisu as the organizers, possibly with one of the invitees trying to twist the tourny into fulfilling some mystical woo-woo for unlimited rice pudding or something? And other &quot;backers&quot; having other agendas.<br /> <br /> Part of me wants to play a slightly-behind-the-curve never-gonna-win-because-he's-not-the-protag beatstick human (Kuwabara, basically). The other part wants to take a theme and play it to the absolute hilt. Like yo-yos. Or candy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T20:05:37-07:00","id":893826,"title":"","content":"As long as somewhere at some point there's a guy watching us fight from a throne, chortling malevolently and intoning things like &quot;Excellent!&quot; I'm in one hundred percent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T20:32:20-07:00","id":893835,"title":"","content":"Oh no worries, that's my default mode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T06:27:17-07:00","id":893972,"title":"","content":"If I play, I would love to play a vampire, a typical Gangrel or Daeva biker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T07:06:24-07:00","id":893990,"title":"","content":"My preference would be Promethean or Hunter, though if we go with 2E that could be more problematic. If pressed I could probably hack something with Mortal Remains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T07:17:40-07:00","id":893997,"title":"","content":"Well, Promethean 2e is in layout now, it should be coming out within the next few months, right? Might be able to finagle the timing such that mechanics aren't needed until after that book drops, or use old mechanics/temporary hack until the new ones come out. (If we're calling dibs, I'd love to have a Changeling, Demon, or human, though I'm happy to compromise.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oooh, new idea, what if each of us played one fighter, and one backer? Not the backer for our own entrant, but someone else's. That'd keep more folks invested longer, probably, although it might also be a logistical headache.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T07:55:15-07:00","id":894016,"title":"","content":"I'm flexible. We'll figure it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T08:36:40-07:00","id":894049,"title":"","content":"If nothing else, I'd like to wait for Hurt Locker to come out so we'll have access to more 2e-compliant combat Merits and hacks. In the mean time, recruiting and brainstorming.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of players as backers. Maybe we could do something like the Pack creation rules from Werewolf where everyone builds a primary character as their team leader, one or more secondary characters as their teammates, and one or more peripheral characters as their team's sponsors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T10:26:28-07:00","id":894144,"title":"","content":"Like I said, I think it would be better to use 1e over 2e simply because there's more published materials for it and less things you have to convert. It would make things easier for the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T10:41:42-07:00","id":894158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=894144#post894144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, I think it would be better to use 1e over 2e simply because there's more published materials for it and less things you have to convert. It would make things easier for the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, there's conversion issues either way - if we play 2e, anyone who wants to play a Geist or a Mummy, or a Z-Splat that hasn't been officially updated will need to rely on converting. If we play 1e, anyone who wants to play a Beast or a Demon will have to rely on back-converting. Ultimately, I think converting from 1e to 2e is easier than back-converting the other way. Another thing to consider is that, without getting into the nebulous idea of &quot;balance&quot;, 1e does have a more significant disparity between the capabilities of different templates. Vampires, for example, would be at a huge disadvantage due to the relatively slow progression of Vitae per turn by Blood Potency compared to other templates' power stats, whereas in 2e this progression is more uniform. And perhaps most importantly for a combat-focused game, 2e's combat rules are much better in my opinion.<br /> <br /> So, I'm leaning pretty heavily towards 2e at this point, but I'm still open to the idea of using 1e if the majority of the players would prefer that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T13:18:29-07:00","id":894274,"title":"","content":"2E is my brew of choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T03:18:04-07:00","id":895404,"title":"","content":"Well, if we're using 2e, I will quietly bow out then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T04:15:18-07:00","id":896678,"title":"","content":"I have a Mage character that'd be perfect for this. Also, count me in on using 2e rules. Combat is much more interesting in 2e, it demands you to think a bit outside the box and constantly use various tactics because straight up attacking seldom works unless there's a huge power gap between characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T08:32:02-07:00","id":897839,"title":"","content":"Count me in. I want to play an Acanthus Arrow. I also prefer 2nd Edition of Mage the Awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T08:38:55-07:00","id":897845,"title":"","content":"Cool, sounds like 2e is definite the crowd favorite option. Like I said earlier, im going to wait for Hurt Locker before I start this, but at this point I definitely think we've got enough interest to see a decent turnout.<br /> <br /> What do folks think about the suggestion of running teams of 1 full character as the team leader, 2 or 3 secondary characters (with partial xp) as teammates, and a peripheral character (with simplified stats) as the team's sponsor? Should players portray their own team's sponsor or another team's?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T12:50:59-07:00","id":898120,"title":"","content":"To be perfectly honest while I like the concept of running multiple different characters I will personally only be able to devote attention to one with my various other commitments out here in meat-world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T15:05:48-07:00","id":898270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=898120#post898120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be perfectly honest while I like the concept of running multiple different characters I will personally only be able to devote attention to one with my various other commitments out here in meat-world.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's reasonable. Perhaps multiple characters could be optional. Maybe we could do something with starting xp so that if you don't have time to focus on multiple characters you're not at a disadvantage against folks with larger teams. That would also make team size more of a tactical consideration - folks can run a standard five-man-band, a single take-all-commers badass, or somewhere inbetween.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T10:22:55-07:00","id":899082,"title":"","content":"I can play multiple characters on multiple teams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T11:43:43-07:00","id":899208,"title":"","content":"Why didn't I look sooner into this? I want to test a werewolf and this seems like the perfect way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T11:46:14-07:00","id":899210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=899208#post899208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why didn't I look sooner into this? I want to test a werewolf and this seems like the perfect way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still plenty of room if you're interested!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T11:47:28-07:00","id":899211,"title":"","content":"Count me in. Anything we can do in the meantime till we wait for Hurt Locker?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:21:54-07:00","id":899248,"title":"","content":"We should definitely work on hammering out the rules of engagement. I'm pretty sure we can all agree, for example, that Mages with Death 5 just straight up instakilling all of their opponents is against the spirit of the competition. While it is very Dark Tournament to have fights be to the death, we might not want that here. I'm thinking I might just use the DT's standard win condition - if a combatant is knocked prone or out of the ring, they have a 10 count (3 turns, with the 10th second being the start of the 4th turn) to get back up or re-enter the ring or they are disqualified. Using Hurt Locker range band rules, I'd think the ring could be Medium range from the center to the outer edge, Long range from end to end, with an out-of-bounds zone at Long range from the center of the ring, Extreme range from the out-of-bounds area on the opposite side (and extending these boundaries upwards for combatants capable of flight).<br /> <br /> Since different templates have different strengths and weaknesses, I'm thinking we should allow team leaders to agree to terms for the match, such as whether it be a series of one-on-one rounds or larger group combat, 3 out of 5 or elimination, etc. and any alternate win conditions they want to establish, such as first blood or what have you. There should be a default to fall back on if an agreement can't be reached (I'm thinking 3 out of 5 one on one rounds.)<br /> <br /> There' also the question of Beaten Down and Surrender. On the one hand, I feel like a fighting tournament is a pretty clear case where both parties' intent is to enact violence on the other, so Beaten Down probably shouldn't apply. Besides that, some templates are immune to the Tilt while others aren't. On the other hand, fighting through being Beaten Down is pretty thematically appropriate for the genre. Maybe Intent should be one of the terms agreed to before the match, with the default being violence for its own sake.<br /> <br /> Are there Sleepers in the audience? If so, how many? I'm leaning towards none, but I'm open to suggestions.<br /> <br /> How about starting experiences? I've found that 20 is a good amount for making characters capable but not too bananas. Then again, in this genre bananas is kind of something to strive for. Characters starting out at reasonable levels and getting gonzo by the final round is also pretty genre appropriate, maybe we should award experiences to victorious teams. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> I'm just kind of throwing ideas against the wall here. I'm open to any other ideas or suggestions. I kind of want this to be a community thing, more than a me calling all the shots thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T15:18:30-07:00","id":899447,"title":"","content":"Awarding full experiences so advancement skyrockets seems genre appropiate. We could keep Beaten Down but maybe changing the trigger, like sufering Wound Penalties, for example. So you'll still need to bash your enemy a lot, but killing is not neccesary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T15:58:31-07:00","id":899494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=899447#post899447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awarding full experiences so advancement skyrockets seems genre appropiate. We could keep Beaten Down but maybe changing the trigger, like sufering Wound Penalties, for example. So you'll still need to bash your enemy a lot, but killing is not neccesary.</div> </div> </div> </div>By full experiences, do you mean an experience any time you would normally recieve a Beat? I like the sound of that. For Beaten Down, how about bumping up the required damage type? (Stamina lethal or any agg)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T16:24:08-07:00","id":899518,"title":"","content":"Tangentially, Charly, have you read Battle Angel Alita? At least up to the Angel of Victory?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T17:29:31-07:00","id":899575,"title":"","content":"I haven't, why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T17:58:08-07:00","id":899592,"title":"","content":"Well, 1) Because Battle Angel Alita is an amazing manga series, you should check it out in general, and 2) For ideas on variety, the sport of Motor Ball should be among the ingredients in the pot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T18:11:51-07:00","id":899603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=899592#post899592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, 1) Because Battle Angel Alita is an amazing manga series, you should check it out in general, and 2) For ideas on variety, the sport of Motor Ball should be among the ingredients in the pot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, I will check it out while we wait!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T19:49:29-07:00","id":899677,"title":"","content":"Sort of a structural question: If one's fighter-character loses a match are they eliminated forever or do they move down into a loser bracket? Obviously they could still hang out and interact with the plot even if eliminated, but as someone who's actually kind of shit at optimization I'm curious how many opportunities we'll have in the ring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T19:58:07-07:00","id":899680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=899677#post899677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sort of a structural question: If one's fighter-character loses a match are they eliminated forever or do they move down into a loser bracket? Obviously they could still hang out and interact with the plot even if eliminated, but as someone who's actually kind of shit at optimization I'm curious how many opportunities we'll have in the ring.</div> </div> </div> </div>We could do it <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swiss-system_tournament\" target=\"_blank\">Swiss style</a> instead of single elimination if folks don't want to be bumped out after one loss. Single elimination is more dramatic, but Swiss insures more players get to participate in more fights.<br /> <br /> A possible compromise could be to have matches between the highest ranking teams be &quot;featured matches&quot; that have more live spectators and a ref (that is to say, me) present, while the non-featured matches could be held more informally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar