tions all around him. Its fake its Hollywood its special effects. That whats his handlers keep feeding him anyways.<br /> <br /> no templates straight human<br /> page302 merits<br /> Communal Sleeper<br /> Lair<br /> <br /> maxout resistant stats<br /> Good Brawl build<br /> <br /> This would be a threat I'd throw at mages. Its a one trick pony. but the trick is to make the character tricks less powerful/useful. Yes the comedic relief is kind of useful sometimes. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a character you're considering playing? Cause I'm definitely into this concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T15:01:17-07:00","id":900395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=899940#post899940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could always have the team matches take place after the individual matches, then there's some drafting and politicking going on over who comprises the teams based on their performance in the individual matches.</div> </div> </div> </div>So like single match preliminaries and forming teams based on the results? That's a cool idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T19:41:40-07:00","id":900582,"title":"","content":"Basically yeah. Seemed like another way to let people fight more than once, introduce some different fight formats, and allow for some RP around the actual forming of the teams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T22:12:12-07:00","id":900694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=900582#post900582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically yeah. Seemed like another way to let people fight more than once, introduce some different fight formats, and allow for some RP around the actual forming of the teams.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that sounds awesome! I'm down for that suggestion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T06:45:30-07:00","id":900902,"title":"","content":"So here's sort of an odd but important question. What are the stakes? Obviously we're all going to be participating in the tournament regardless and the casus belli is mostly a flimsy justification to facilitate dudes fighting a bunch, but what is the prize to keep one's eyes on? Money? Power? Magical MacGuffins? The Fate of the Universe<span style=\"font-size:8px\">TM</span><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">?</span></span><br /> <br /> Of course I'm also assuming we'll meet our necessary quota of &quot;I must fight to be the very best and strongest because I am compelled to test my limits and martial <i>virtus</i> demands it.&quot; along with &quot;Pursuing secret vendetta against tournament organizers or another competitor because entering the same fighting competition as them is the most direct and least contrived method of assassination.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:24:50-07:00","id":900993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=900902#post900902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here's sort of an odd but important question. What are the stakes? Obviously we're all going to be participating in the tournament regardless and the casus belli is mostly a flimsy justification to facilitate dudes fighting a bunch, but what is the prize to keep one's eyes on? Money? Power? Magical MacGuffins? The Fate of the Universe<span style=\"font-size:8px\">TM</span><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">?</span></span><br /> <br /> Of course I'm also assuming we'll meet our necessary quota of &quot;I must fight to be the very best and strongest because I am compelled to test my limits and martial <i>virtus</i> demands it.&quot; along with &quot;Pursuing secret vendetta against tournament organizers or another competitor because entering the same fighting competition as them is the most direct and least contrived method of assassination.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we discussed this a little bit earlier, thouh we were somewhat non-specific on the details. Basically with the Hototogisu orchestrating the event and some of the most powerful supernatural creatures in Tokyo backing it, they can pool their resources to meet nearly any reward the winners desire. Within some reasonable limits, of course, but if you want money or temporal power, they've got you covered. If you want immortality (though of course, many contestants will already have it), that can probably be arranged. If you want your ailing or deceased loved one restored to health or life, that should be a simple matter. If you want to possess the long-lost McGuffan of Vaguely Defined Power, it might take some time to acquire but shouldn't be beyond the reach of the tournament committee. Basically they would advertised it as granting any single request that is within the committe's considerable power to fulfill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T15:50:12-07:00","id":901481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=900993#post900993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we discussed this a little bit earlier, thouh we were somewhat non-specific on the details. Basically with the Hototogisu orchestrating the event and some of the most powerful supernatural creatures in Tokyo backing it, they can pool their resources to meet nearly any reward the winners desire. Within some reasonable limits, of course, but if you want money or temporal power, they've got you covered. If you want immortality (though of course, many contestants will already have it), that can probably be arranged. If you want your ailing or deceased loved one restored to health or life, that should be a simple matter. If you want to possess the long-lost McGuffan of Vaguely Defined Power, it might take some time to acquire but shouldn't be beyond the reach of the tournament committee. Basically they would advertised it as granting any single request that is within the committe's considerable power to fulfill.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is gonna be an OCT plot, I know it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T12:09:28-07:00","id":908493,"title":"","content":"What's the starting XP? Because my concept work best as a second-degree Adept, with Honorary Rank and Sever Oath, but can work simply as Fox-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T14:00:57-07:00","id":908590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=908493#post908493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the starting XP? Because my concept work best as a second-degree Adept, with Honorary Rank and Sever Oath, but can work simply as Fox-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the only 2e game I've run with starting experiences was vampire using Climbing the Ladder, so I'm not sure what works well. In my 1e experience, I found 100 to be a good number for starting out appreciably powerful but not ridiculous. In 2e, that would be 20 experiences. Does that sound like a good amount, keeping in mind we are probably doing turbo-advancement by granting full Experiences in place of Beats?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T17:52:30-07:00","id":908758,"title":"","content":"Sounds fine to me. I imagine we'll discover quickly that splats benefit from Experiences in different ways and some probably benefit moreso on a point to point basis than others, but we aren't here for white room balance we're here for a re-stonking-donkulous martial arts tournament.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T04:06:12-07:00","id":909024,"title":"","content":"Well said. So 20 xp, uh? Now I can start character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T06:02:10-07:00","id":909086,"title":"","content":"*steeples fingers* Eeeexcellent<br /> <br /> Question: for splats that have 2e versions currently in production, should we wait to build them, use whatever spoiled rules we can, or start at 1e and convert later? For Promethean, it may be wiser to wait, since it's hovering at layout; for Changeling, it's earlier in the cycle but has semi-solid spoiled rules for the majority of the pieces, meaning using the spoiled rules may be smartest.<br /> <br /> (part of me wants to build a &quot;Drac Pack&quot; that's made up of Beasts that are all dragons but from different families. another part wants to build a &quot;Drak Pack&quot; that's made up of dragons from different splats (Beast, Changeling, Demon, Vampire, skinchanger)).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T07:04:18-07:00","id":909135,"title":"","content":"I'm leaning towards a cautionary tale of a Cheiron Group hunter so far down the rabbit hole of Thaumatech he's more monster parts than mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T08:06:12-07:00","id":909172,"title":"","content":"20 experience points, I'm creating now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T09:44:29-07:00","id":909230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=909086#post909086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*steeples fingers* Eeeexcellent<br /> <br /> Question: for splats that have 2e versions currently in production, should we wait to build them, use whatever spoiled rules we can, or start at 1e and convert later? For Promethean, it may be wiser to wait, since it's hovering at layout; for Changeling, it's earlier in the cycle but has semi-solid spoiled rules for the majority of the pieces, meaning using the spoiled rules may be smartest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, go with the spoiled playtest material for Changelings. Use the conversion notes from Mortal Remains for Hunters. Wait out Prometheans and see if the book comes out before Hurt Locker does. For Geists and Mummies, build with 1e rules. 100xp instead of 20, average out scaling experience costs (so Merits are 6xp per dot instead of 2xp xNew Dot), and power stat costs 25xp per dot and costs 5 starting Merit dots instead of 3. Use 2e for non splat-specific Merits and start with 10 free dots instead of 7.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-07-2016, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T16:36:25-07:00","id":912515,"title":"","content":"This looks to be very much my jam. So I'm in if there is still room.<br /> <br /> I haven't seen it brought up in the thread yet but what (if any) weapons would it be appropriate to arm a character with?<br /> <br /> Guns would seem a bit genre inappropriate but they're about on par with some of the supernatural powers others are going to be able to throw around.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T17:22:51-07:00","id":912540,"title":"","content":"There's definitely still room! As far as I'm concerned we can't have too many players.<br /> <br /> As for weapons, I think that should be one of the terms agreed to by the team leaders before a fight. By default I wouldn't put any restrictions on weapons.<br /> <br /> Specific to firearms though, I should note that I plan to use the Range Bands and Ammo Capacity rules that were previewed from Hurt Locker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T14:01:17-07:00","id":912984,"title":"","content":"Wait, this is happening?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T14:13:54-07:00","id":912992,"title":"","content":"I'm still planning to wait for Hurt Locker to come out, but yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T07:13:24-07:00","id":913367,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I can't wait to see what a Master of Fate can do in this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T07:49:58-07:00","id":913378,"title":"","content":"Relevant question: Will combat be strictly unarmed or will weapons be allowed? If so, what kinds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T08:08:39-07:00","id":913383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=913378#post913378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Relevant question: Will combat be strictly unarmed or will weapons be allowed? If so, what kinds?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=912540#post912540\">Boop</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T12:18:06-07:00","id":913573,"title":"","content":"To clarify: this is a team tournament, with 5 beings on a team, yeah? Is the 20xp split up among them, or each? If I wanted to submit a 3-being team, or a 1-being team, could I reconfigure the xp between them, or is it &quot;always 20xp per being, run a smaller team at your own risk&quot;? Or should we just have single characters, then have them choose teams? (I personally like 5-being team, 20xp each, dropping a team member gives you 20xp to spread around your remaining members, but IDK if having one being at 100xp would be game-breakingly unfun...)<br /> <br /> Also, presumably there's a tourney rule of no attacks outside of rounds, meaning my Changeling shouldn't dream-torment her opponents to eat up their Willpower before the match. Or should it be allowed? Maybe each team gets one between-round action each, where they can choose between finding out information, antagonizing the other team, buffing themselves, etc, based on their own innate abilities.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Maybe this would be fairer: each solo contestant gets 20xp. For multi-being teams, reduce each being's xp by 5 for each member above one. So 1-being team: 20xp. 2-being team: 15xp (each). 3-being team: 10xp (each). 4-being team: 5xp (each). 5-being team: 0xp (each).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":". 06-13-2016, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T12:54:18-07:00","id":913601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=913573#post913573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify: this is a team tournament, with 5 beings on a team, yeah? Is the 20xp split up among them, or each? If I wanted to submit a 3-being team, or a 1-being team, could I reconfigure the xp between them, or is it &amp;quot;always 20xp per being, run a smaller team at your own risk&amp;quot;? Or should we just have single characters, then have them choose teams? (I personally like 5-being team, 20xp each, dropping a team member gives you 20xp to spread around your remaining members, but IDK if having one being at 100xp would be game-breakingly unfun...)</div> </div> </div> </div>My thinking is 1 team leader, 4 other teammates, and a sponsor. Your team leader is built with normal character creation rules plus 20 experiences. Other teammates are built using the secondary pack member rules from Werewolf (5/4/3 for Attributes, 15 dots in Skills, 5 dots in Merits) plus 5 experiences each. Sponsor is made with the peripheral pack member rules from werewolf (three dice pools, one at 5, one at 4, and one at 3, 2 dots of Willpower). If you want to have fewer members on your team, you can see if anyone else would like to play any of your team members, or distribute any missing members' experiences between the remaining members.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=913573#post913573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, presumably there's a tourney rule of no attacks outside of rounds, meaning my Changeling shouldn't dream-torment her opponents to eat up their Willpower before the match. Or should it be allowed? Maybe each team gets one between-round action each, where they can choose between finding out information, antagonizing the other team, buffing themselves, etc, based on their own innate abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely want to include downtime actions between matches. I figure that will mostly be where the team sponsors come into play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T13:05:06-07:00","id":913610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=913601#post913601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thinking is 1 team leader, 4 other teammates, and a sponsor. Your team leader is built with normal character creation rules plus 20 experiences. Other teammates are built using the secondary pack member rules from Werewolf (5/4/3 for Attributes, 15 dots in Skills, 5 dots in Merits) plus 5 experiences each. Sponsor is made with the peripheral pack member rules from werewolf (three dice pools, one at 5, one at 4, and one at 3, 2 dots of Willpower). If you want to have fewer members on your team, you can see if anyone else would like to play any of your team members, or distribute any missing members' experiences between the remaining members.<br /> <br /> <br /> I definitely want to include downtime actions between matches. I figure that will mostly be where the team sponsors come into play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha, okay. For &quot;other teammates&quot;, what are the rules on supernatural powers? I.E. would a vampire get 3 Discipline dots? Would a changeling get 5 Contract dots? If yes, are they restricted at all? If no, presumably they could be bought with the 5xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T13:51:56-07:00","id":913637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=913610#post913610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gotcha, okay. For &amp;quot;other teammates&amp;quot;, what are the rules on supernatural powers? I.E. would a vampire get 3 Discipline dots? Would a changeling get 5 Contract dots? If yes, are they restricted at all? If no, presumably they could be bought with the 5xp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... Probably go with what ever the default starting powers for the template are, and yes they can be bought with experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T14:20:39-07:00","id":913649,"title":"","content":"So I'm currently thinking a group of Japanese idol singer Werewolves (members of 36Love from the Tokyo section of WtF 2E) as my team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T14:32:43-07:00","id":913657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=913649#post913649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm currently thinking a group of Japanese idol singer Werewolves (members of 36Love from the Tokyo section of WtF 2E) as my team.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! The plan is to set the game in Tokyo, so that should work well. I take it you'll be playing as one of the 4-member cells from outside the city?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T15:09:51-07:00","id":913682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/889231-gauging-interest-chronicles-of-dark-tournament?p=913657#post913657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awesome! The plan is to set the game in Tokyo, so that should work well. I take it you'll be playing as one of the 4-member cells from outside the city?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's my base plan right now with a wolf blooded publicity agent acting as their sponsor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title